- **Premise**: index is between 0 and the initial size inclusive → `index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size())`
- **Quantified range**: for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size → `index <= i && i <= \old(this.size())`
- **Property**: the element at each such index in the updated list is either null (and the corresponding previous-index element was null in the old list), or equals the element at the previous index in the old list → `(this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i-1)) == null) || (this.get(i) != null && this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1))))`

The null-case handling is needed because `.equals` cannot be invoked on a null reference, and the comparison is always against the previous index (`i-1`) in the old list since elements are shifted right by one.

