Looking at the comment, I need to break it down:

- **Premise:** "If the index is between 0 and the initial size of the list inclusive" → `index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size())`
- **Quantification:** "for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list" → valid old indices `i` with `index <= i < \old(this.size())` (the elements being shifted). The "subsequent index in the updated list" is `i+1`, and the "previous index in the old list" is `i`.
- **Property:** "the element at each subsequent index in the updated list is either null and was null in the old list, or is equal to the element at the previous index in the old list" → `(this.get(i+1) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i)))`

The shift moves `old[i]` to `new[i+1]`, so the subsequent index `i+1` ranges up to the old size, matching "to the old size of the list."

<code>assert (index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size())) => (\forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i+1) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i))));</code>
